  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1015 PM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nFriday opens with a backdoor front exiting Oklahoma ahead of cool, \nbut light E-NE winds. NBM looks to have a good handle regarding this \nearlier and cooler push as shown by the HRRR, so its highs in the \n60s across the board fit well despite minimal clouds under an upper \nridge. The upper ridge departs Friday night ahead of a lead \nsouthern stream trough tracking largely along and south of I-20 on\nSaturday. This presents us with some top-down moistening \nopportunities on Saturday, before the more impactful shortwave \ntrough arrives Saturday afternoon and evening with deeper ascent,\nthicker saturation, and modest CAPE for some storms. This lift \ncombined with PWATs of 0.75\" to 0.9\" should allow for some soaking\nrainfall, but flooding concerns are low as the forcing remains \nprogressive.\n\nMid-level subsidence unfolds for Sunday on the back side of a weak \nsurface and upper low which presents us with a tricky scenario for \nclouds and temps. Highs could run the gamut should we see enough dry \nslotting and clearing skies in the south contrasted with another \nbackdoor front farther north which has the potential for highs only \nin the upper 40s. NBM still favors this chilly dome overspreading \nthe entire area Sunday evening with highs on Monday barely cracking \n50 degrees thanks to cool and moist upslope flow laden with stratus \nand maybe some drizzle. These cool winds veer south for Tuesday, yet\nthis alone is unlikely to rid us of low clouds and below-normal highs\nin the lower 50s. Deeper southwest flow aloft then delivers a \nshortwave trough for either late Tuesday or Wednesday complete with\nsome shower chances and slightly milder temps.",
